# Using getSessionCookie for Middleware Protection

Based on the documentation, here's the exact implementation:

## Import and Function Signature

```ts
import { getSessionCookie } from "better-auth/cookies";
```

The function accepts a `NextRequest` object and optional configuration:

```ts
const sessionCookie = getSessionCookie(request);
```

## Complete Example

```ts title="middleware.ts or proxy.ts"
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { getSessionCookie } from "better-auth/cookies";

export async function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
	const sessionCookie = getSessionCookie(request);

	if (!sessionCookie) {
		return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/sign-in", request.url));
	}

	return NextResponse.next();
}

export const config = {
	matcher: ["/dashboard"],
};
```

## Custom Configuration

If you've customized your cookie name or prefix:

```ts
const sessionCookie = getSessionCookie(request, {
    cookieName: "my_session_cookie",
    cookiePrefix: "my_prefix"
});
```

## Important Security Note

The documentation emphasizes that this approach is "optimistic" and "not secure" on its own, as it "only checks for the existence of a session cookie" without validation. Always perform proper session validation on your server for protected actions.

